WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.917
LARRY ARNN: There's a
lot in the ethics that's

00:00:01.917 --> 00:00:03.240
Goldilocks argument.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.460
Not too hot, not too
cold, just right,

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.090
and how do you make a rule
to tell which is which?

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.810
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.548
What is character?

00:00:17.548 --> 00:00:19.590
SPEAKER 1: It's the state
of the soul that arises

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.863
from the choices one makes.

00:00:20.863 --> 00:00:23.280
LARRY ARNN: State of the soul
that arises from the choices

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.510
that you make.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.180
OK, so we're going to try to
figure out how that works,

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.710
and to do that,
we're going to begin

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.660
with the beginning of
Book two of the ethics,

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.410
and if somebody reads
the first paragraph,

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.720
there's some cool
stuff in there.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.570
SPEAKER 2: Now, since virtue
is of two sorts, one pertaining

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.210
to thinking and the
other to character,

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.590
excellence of thinking
is, for the most part,

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.140
both in its coming to
be and in its growth

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:52.590
a result of teaching
for which reason

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.320
it has a need of
experience and time,

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.090
while excellence
of character comes

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.000
into being as a consequence
of habit on account

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.030
of which it even gets its
name by a small inflection

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.410
from habit.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.600
LARRY ARNN: How do you
make a good choice?

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:12.060
No simple answer, but
one thing is the motive.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.810
You have to do it to do
the right thing, especially

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.580
the beautiful thing.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.320
You also have to estimate
the circumstances.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.410
Well, an act is courageous if
it's done for the beautiful,

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.390
unless it's grossly foolish.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:32.010
You can imagine some movie
where some soldier stands

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:37.380
up and charges a whole army
of tanks and gets blown away

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.780
and that's brave in one
way, but in another way,

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.520
it's ridiculous.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.530
So you don't want to
do that, so there's

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.470
a whole bunch of things
that make for a good choice,

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.770
but the point he's
making here is

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:54.090
that you go from
habit to character

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:57.270
by making choices
and making them well,

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.230
and that's what changes you.

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:03.270
And if we don't
make good choices,

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:06.120
it will violate our
nature, but it's not

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.699
natural in the same
sense as our growing

00:02:08.699 --> 00:02:11.830
or as an oak tree
growing is natural.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:15.780
The realm of volition in
which human beings live

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.320
is all important.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.540
You can take 1,000 examples,
they're everywhere.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:27.360
But if you commit vicious acts
often, abuse people, which

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:32.190
will turn you into a tyrant and
you'll be hated and unhappy,

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:36.100
drink to excess, turn you
into a drunk, be unhappy,

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.870
you can do those things.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:41.160
Then you're harming your
nature, whereas if you

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.060
make good choices, you
accord more completely

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.260
with your nature.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.180
But don't mistake
that you are not

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.820
an agent in the doing of it.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.970
There's a lot in the ethics
that Goldilocks argument.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.310
Not too hot, not too
cold, just right.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:00.270
Not too hard, not too soft, and
that's an interesting problem,

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:05.760
because how do you make a
rule to tell which is which?

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.160
How do you know,
and the answer is,

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.940
there isn't any rule
that you can make.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.560
In this case of
training, it's not

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.190
too hard to know that if you
run until you're exhausted

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.230
and your shins hurt and
you can't run anymore,

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.430
then you've run too much.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.700
And if you don't run
enough and you're

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.710
exhausted when you start
and you can't keep up,

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.180
you haven't trained enough.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.630
Take moderation.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:33.210
There isn't any iron rule.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.580
You're seeking a right amount.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:41.460
Indeed, it's the business of
life to seek the right amount,

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:47.940
and there's all these obstacles
and temptations and confusions

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:51.670
that are in the way, but
if you think about it

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:55.330
and you keep your soul in order
and you keep your direction,

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:59.940
your attitude right, then
you'll make better choices,

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:03.840
and Aristotle is saying that's
how you hone in on this.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:09.150
And another point to understand
is it gets easier while you go.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.270
Is school easier than
when you started?

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.510
Yeah, you probably showed
up, wow, this is awful.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.430
Can't do this.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.519
Now you can't, it's just hard.

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:23.280
So you see what you've gained.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.070
You have a better soul
than you had before.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:32.820
So that point then is don't
underestimate what you know,

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.630
and the whole question of choice
is going to hang on this thing

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.890
that, in your heart
of hearts, you know.

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:44.070
And if you choose against
that consistently,

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:47.950
that is the only way
to silence that voice.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:51.630
And if you listen to that
voice, it will become strong

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:55.580
and it will drown
out everything else.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:05:00.590
That is the specific action
of character building.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:01.610
That's what it does.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.910
I'm Larry Arnn, president
of Hillsdale College.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:10.400
You will find if you look
at our online courses

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:13.040
that they cover the whole
range of human learning,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.520
all the high and fundamental
things everyone needs to know.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.800
They are free,
because we have always

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.770
wished to provide sound
learning to anyone

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:24.070
who wishes to have it.

